* Terminal order for both stages: noninverting, inverting, output, V+, V-, common.
* The 2520 is the base circuit of the published reverse-engineered "API 2520 OpAmp".
* The notes on that drawing describe other variants. This subcircuit uses the drawn one.
.subckt DOA2520_DRAWN ip im out vp vn com
Q1 q1c ip tail A525_MATCH_N
Q2 q2c im tail A525_MATCH_N
Q3 q3c q2c front_tail A525_TIS98
Q4 q4c q1c front_tail A525_TIS98
Q5 bias_lower sink_ctl q5e A525_TIS98
Q6 sink_ctl q4c q6e A525_2N5087
Q7 vp driver_upper q7e A525_2N3053
Q8 vn bias_lower q8e A525_2N4036
Q9 bias_upper q3c driver_upper A525_2N5087
R1 tail vn 150k
R2 q1c r2_ac 100
R3 vp q1c 82k
R4 vp trim_tap 22k
R5 trim_tap q2c 68k
R6 vp q3c 3k
R7 vp q4c 3.9k
R8 vp q6e 1k
R9 vp driver_upper 56
R10 q9_ac bias_upper 800
R11 q7e out 5.6
R12 out q8e 5.6
R13 q5e vn 56
R14 sink_ctl q5_ac 1k
R15 sink_ctl vn 1k
R16 front_tail sink_ctl 47k
C1 r2_ac q2c 1000p
C2 q3c q9_ac 47p
C3 q5_ac bias_lower 47p
C4 vp q1c 39p
C5 q2c bias_lower 47p
D1 bias_upper bias_lower A525_MZ2361
D2 out driver_upper A525_MZ2361
D3 bias_lower out A525_MZ2361
.ends DOA2520_DRAWN

* Q9 diagnostic variant: the base drive comes from the Q9 collector.
* R9 remains at the original value and is in the Q9 emitter leg.
* Engineering interpretation of the redraw, pending a corroborating trace.
.subckt DOA2520_Q9_CORE ip im out vp vn c5_return q2c params: c5_value=47p
Q1 q1c ip tail A525_MATCH_N
Q2 q2c im tail A525_MATCH_N
Q3 q3c q2c front_tail A525_TIS98
Q4 q4c q1c front_tail A525_TIS98
Q5 bias_lower sink_ctl q5e A525_TIS98
Q6 sink_ctl q4c q6e A525_2N5087
Q7 vp driver_upper q7e A525_2N3053
Q8 vn bias_lower q8e A525_2N4036
Q9 driver_upper q3c q9e A525_2N5087
R1 tail vn 150k
R2 q1c r2_ac 100
R3 vp q1c 82k
R4 vp trim_tap 22k
R5 trim_tap q2c 68k
R6 vp q3c 3k
R7 vp q4c 3.9k
R8 vp q6e 1k
R9 vp q9e 56
R10 q9_ac driver_upper 800
R11 q7e out 5.6
R12 out q8e 5.6
R13 q5e vn 56
R14 sink_ctl q5_ac 1k
R15 sink_ctl vn 1k
R16 front_tail sink_ctl 47k
C1 r2_ac q2c 1000p
C2 q3c q9_ac 47p
C3 q5_ac bias_lower 47p
C4 vp q1c 39p
C5 c5_return bias_lower {c5_value}
D1 driver_upper bias_lower A525_MZ2361
D2 out driver_upper A525_MZ2361
D3 bias_lower out A525_MZ2361
.ends DOA2520_Q9_CORE

* Preserve the original connection for A/B diagnostics.
.subckt DOA2520_Q9_TEST ip im out vp vn com
Xcore ip im out vp vn q2c q2c DOA2520_Q9_CORE
.ends DOA2520_Q9_TEST

* Alternative C5 placement at the inverting input. The builders' -IN and
* 10 pF reports are design leads; this combination is not an API-verified card.
.subckt DOA2520_10P ip im out vp vn com
Xcore ip im out vp vn im q2c DOA2520_Q9_CORE c5_value=10p
.ends DOA2520_10P

* Jensen Fig. 6, original JE-990, with R10 and R11 for +/-15 V.
* Raw output is the feedback node. The application-dependent isolator is separate.
.subckt JE990_15 ip im out vp vn com
Q1 mirror_ref im q1e A525_LM394_HALF
Q2 vas_in ip q2e A525_LM394_HALF
Q3 vas_in mirror_ref q3e A525_2N4250A
Q4 tail tail_bias q4e A525_2N2484
Q5 vn vas_in vas_drive A525_2N4250A
Q6 bias_high vas_drive q6e A525_2N4250A
Q7 bias_low sink_bias q7e A525_2N2484
Q8 vp bias_high q8e A525_MJE181
Q9 vn bias_low q9e A525_MJE171
R1 q1e tail 30
R2 tail q2e 30
R3 q4e vn 160
R4 vp mirror_emitter 300
R5 vp q3e 300
R6 vp vas_drive 2k
R7 vp q6e 180
R8 vp hf_damp 300
R9 vas_in comp_ac 130
R10 vp tail_bias 33k
R11 vp sink_bias 33k
R12 q7e vn 110
R13 q8e out 3.9
R14 out q9e 3.9
C1 comp_ac comp_diode 150p
C2 vp q6e 62p
C3 hf_damp q6e 91p
C4 vp com .1u
C5 com vn .1u
L1 q1e tail 20u
L2 q2e tail 20u
DCR1 im ip A525_1N914B
DCR2 ip im A525_1N914B
DCR3 mirror_emitter mirror_ref A525_1N914B
DCR4 bias_high comp_diode A525_1N914B
DCR5 tail_bias cr56 A525_1N914B
DCR6 cr56 vn A525_1N914B
DCR7 sink_bias cr78 A525_1N914B
DCR8 cr78 vn A525_1N914B
DCR9 bias_high bias_mid A525_1N914B
DCR10 bias_mid bias_low A525_1N914B
DCR11 out bias_high A525_1N914B
DCR12 bias_low out A525_1N914B
.ends JE990_15

.subckt JE990_ISOLATOR feedback output
R15 feedback output 39
L3 feedback output 40u
.ends JE990_ISOLATOR
